WHATNOW

What tam-idol is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-26, with W19


STATE

  Version 1.3.0 on branch dev (1.0.0 tagged 1.0.0 / v1.0.0 on Fred's
  word). The standard is written down: README has the standard set and the
  procedures, arch/layout.md the list that tools/idol-check checks,
  arch/roadmap.md the ROADMAP.md standard (W19), and
  each README-<folder> the text that every repository copies above its
  IN THIS REPOSITORY section.

  keys/keybindings.md is the shared keybinding standard. Programs
  document their own bindings in keys/keybindings.md (with
  keys/README-keys) and link to the standard there (W17, W18).

  The initial rollout covered these repositories: tam-clif (W1),
  tam-file (W2), tam-clam (W3), tam-pane (W4), tam-last (W5), tam-data
  (W6), tam-view, tam-bud, tam-ring (W9), tam-edit (W10), libtam (W11),
  tam (W12), tamlinux-tools (W13), and tamlinux (W14).

  D272's branch rename (W7), D278's docs/ai/ retirement (W8), "Blame
  everywhere" across every repository including tam (W14), and the
  tamlinux survey and reorganization (W14) are all complete on dev.
  References to the renamed tam-clif repository were updated (W16).


NEXT

  1. When a repository shows the standard is wrong or missing something,
     change tam-idol first, bump VERSION, and say why in ROADMAP.md.
  2. Start every new repository from tam-idol and verify it with
     tools/idol-check.
  3. Use the shared keybinding standard when updating a program's
     input layer.


